\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l198k2jr/8019ca22-b341-420c-9637-2162f155fd82/5a5dcf70-adc6-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l198k2js.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l198k2jr/8019ca22-b341-420c-9637-2162f155fd82/5a5dcf70-adc6-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l198k2js.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l198k2jr/8019ca22-b341-420c-9637-2162f155fd82/5a5dcf70-adc6-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l198k2js.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l198k2jr/8019ca22-b341-420c-9637-2162f155fd82/5a5dcf70-adc6-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l198k2js.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l198k2jr/8019ca22-b341-420c-9637-2162f155fd82/5a5dcf70-adc6-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l198k2js.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l198k2jr/8019ca22-b341-420c-9637-2162f155fd82/5a5dcf70-adc6-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l198k2js.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>For [Ti(H<sub>2</sub>O)<sub>5</sub>Cl](NO<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub>,</p>\n<p> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l198xs02/401f2ac9-7ada-4d55-bd34-c5659579a087/d78c0e20-adc7-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l198xs03.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l198xs02/401f2ac9-7ada-4d55-bd34-c5659579a087/d78c0e20-adc7-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l198xs03.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 38 English Explanation 2\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l198xs02/401f2ac9-7ada-4d55-bd34-c5659579a087/d78c0e20-adc7-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l198xs03.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l198xs02/401f2ac9-7ada-4d55-bd34-c5659579a087/d78c0e20-adc7-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l198xs03.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l198xs02/401f2ac9-7ada-4d55-bd34-c5659579a087/d78c0e20-adc7-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l198xs03.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l198xs02/401f2ac9-7ada-4d55-bd34-c5659579a087/d78c0e20-adc7-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l198xs03.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l198xs02/401f2ac9-7ada-4d55-bd34-c5659579a087/d78c0e20-adc7-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l198xs03.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l198xs02/401f2ac9-7ada-4d55-bd34-c5659579a087/d78c0e20-adc7-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l198xs03.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>The complex is paramagnetic due to presence of unpaired electron.</p>\n<p>Since the groups between the complex ion and ions outside can be exchanged, it shows ionisation isomerism.</p>\n<p>For [Pt(en)(NH<sub>3</sub>)Cl]NO<sub>3</sub>,</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l198z824/a2f81857-bff3-42fe-8ad2-4a668509e0c0/ffc28cc0-adc7-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l198z825.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l198z824/a2f81857-bff3-42fe-8ad2-4a668509e0c0/ffc28cc0-adc7-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l198z825.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 38 English Explanation 3\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l198z824/a2f81857-bff3-42fe-8ad2-4a668509e0c0/ffc28cc0-adc7-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l198z825.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l198z824/a2f81857-bff3-42fe-8ad2-4a668509e0c0/ffc28cc0-adc7-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l198z825.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l198z824/a2f81857-bff3-42fe-8ad2-4a668509e0c0/ffc28cc0-adc7-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l198z825.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l198z824/a2f81857-bff3-42fe-8ad2-4a668509e0c0/ffc28cc0-adc7-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l198z825.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l198z824/a2f81857-bff3-42fe-8ad2-4a668509e0c0/ffc28cc0-adc7-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l198z825.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l198z824/a2f81857-bff3-42fe-8ad2-4a668509e0c0/ffc28cc0-adc7-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l198z825.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>The complex is square planar and all electrons are paired. So it is diamagnetic. Since the groups between the complex ion and ions outside can be exchanged, it shows ionisation isomerism.</p>\n<p>For [Co(NH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>4</sub>(NO<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub>]NO<sub>3</sub>, NH<sub>3</sub> is a strong ligand and causes pairing</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l19908l0/5e5a74c1-655b-44c2-a074-375a6e547119/1bf99a50-adc8-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l19908l1.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l19908l0/5e5a74c1-655b-44c2-a074-375a6e547119/1bf99a50-adc8-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l19908l1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 38 English Explanation 4\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l19908l0/5e5a74c1-655b-44c2-a074-375a6e547119/1bf99a50-adc8-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l19908l1.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l19908l0/5e5a74c1-655b-44c2-a074-375a6e547119/1bf99a50-adc8-11ec-87cf-6f66ef86ef1e/file-1l19908l1.png?format=png 750w, http